<title>HONG KONG: Special beer brewed to mark Hong Kong handover.</title>
<headline>Special beer brewed to mark Hong Kong handover.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's handover to China is to be marked by a Red Dawn.</p>
<p>The South China Brewing Company has produced a special &quot;Red Dawn&quot; lager for celebrations heralding the end of 156 years of Brtitish colonial rule in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>It is decorated with '97 labels and the red flag of China folding over Britain's Union Jack.</p>
<p>The South China Morning Post, giving its verdict on the beer, concluded: &quot;When you wake up from a drunken stupor sometime on July 1, it's good to have the label on hand to remind you that you are no longer in the British territory.&quot;</p>
</text>
